# Hide and Seek: AI-Powered 2D Stealth Game 🎮🤖

**Bachelor's Thesis Project (B.Sc. in Telecommunications Technologies and Systems)**  
*Technical University of Cluj-Napoca (UTCN)*

## 📝 Overview
This project is a 2D educational stealth game developed in Python using the Pygame library. The core innovation of this project is the integration of a **local Large Language Model (LLM)** to dynamically influence NPC (Non-Player Character) behavior and game states. 

Instead of relying on basic scripted events, the game queries a local AI model (Llama 3.2 via Ollama). To handle the computational weight of local AI inference without breaking the game loop, the architecture utilizes **asynchronous multithreading**, strict **JSON validation**, and a hardcoded **deterministic fallback system**.

## ✨ Key Features
*   **Local AI Integration:** Utilizes Ollama to run large language models locally, processing game events and dictating NPC decisions without requiring an internet connection.
*   **Asynchronous Multithreading:** The heavy AI inference runs on a background daemon thread. This completely decouples the AI processing from the main game loop, ensuring the UI/rendering runs smoothly at 60 FPS without freezing.
*   **Robust Fallback System (Defensive Programming):** AI outputs are non-deterministic. The game features a strict JSON validation layer that intercepts malformed or hallucinated AI responses and replaces them with a safe, hardcoded default state to prevent application crashes.
*   **Advanced Game AI:**
    *   **A* Pathfinding Algorithm:** Calculates the shortest and most efficient path for NPCs to navigate complex maps.
    *   **Finite State Machine (FSM):** Manages NPC behavioral states (e.g., Idle, Patrol, Chase, Search).
    *   **Field of View (FOV) & Line of Sight:** Implements raycasting/grid-based visibility so NPCs only react to what they can "see" within their cone of vision.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
*   **Programming Language:** Python 3.x
*   **Game Engine/Graphics:** Pygame
*   **AI Backend:** Ollama (Llama 3.2 model)
*   **Core Concepts Used:** Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), Multithreading, JSON Parsing & Validation, Graph Search Algorithms (A*).

## 🚀 Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites
1.  **Python 3.x:** Ensure Python is installed on your system.
2.  **Ollama:** You must have [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) installed to run the local AI model.

### Steps
1. **Clone the repository:**
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/DimaRobert-Andrei/hide-and-seek-ai.git](https://github.com/DimaRobert-Andrei/hide-and-seek-ai.git)
   cd hide-and-seek-ai
Install Python dependencies:

Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
(Note: Ensure pygame is included in your environment).

Start the local AI model:
Open a terminal and run the following command to start the Ollama server with the Llama 3.2 model:

Bash
ollama run llama3.2
Run the game:
Open a new terminal window and start the game script:

Bash
python main.py
🧠 Architecture Highlights
During development, dealing with hardware constraints and unpredictable API responses was a major challenge.

The UI Bottleneck: Synchronous API calls to the LLM caused severe frame drops. This was resolved by implementing a multithreaded queue system.

Data Integrity: The LLM occasionally returned invalid JSON formats. I engineered a parsing layer that attempts to reconstruct broken JSON and, if it fails, gracefully defaults to a safe fallback state, ensuring the game never crashes due to bad AI outputs.

